### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)
- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).
- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.
- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.
- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.
