.temp/TASK-260830-2h5uv9/board-readback/TASK-260830-2h5uv9_results.md:83:The complete `(package, entry, input)` grid, base/candidate moved classes, and graph diff are in `TASK-260830-2h5uv9_conformance-matrix.md`, the attached `IMPORTER-OUTCOMES.md` in the evidence archive, and `graph-diff.md`. The refreshed grid includes `internal/tmuxserver` → `provhost.CreateIdentity` for its ordinary test identity fixture; that test-only edge and fixture exist on both sides, and both package runs pass. The base and candidate package sets each ran in full: 45/45 and 46/46 respectively. The generated candidate test ran separately in all 38,000 cases. Moved classes are named: Section 10.7 Tombstone and Acknowledgement identity shapes move from fail-closed to validated admission; durable sync adds immutable union, delayed-gap recovery, same-ID byte conflict quarantine/abort and repository-bound projection; lease tuple derivation ignores timestamp ordering; and registry cases/report coverage change. The graphs show no removed or redirected pre-existing edge. Full package-suite results establish package tests pass on both sides; they do not establish semantic equality for every possible input to every unchanged importer.
